{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inherited from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence.Iterator"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Iterator"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/St","doc:\/\/Cliques\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Cliques\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Iterator"}],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Cliques"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques.swift#L327","fileName":"MaximalCliques.swift"},"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V8IteratorV","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Iterator","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MaximalCliques.Iterator","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Iterator","kind":"identifier"}]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/iterator"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Iterator\/next()"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","title":"MaximalCliques","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/Iterator":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/iterator","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Iterator","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Iterator","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MaximalCliques.Iterator","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/Iterator"},"doc://Cliques/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/s8SendableP"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/Iterator/next()":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/iterator\/next()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"ke